  "caption": "Quinn copied a pro lifter's program, piled on the plates, and felt a twinge on the last set of week three.\n\nMost heavy-lifting aches are strains or overload rather than structural damage. The usual story is load, volume or frequency rising faster than recovery, not one bad rep.\n\nWhat can help: add weight gradually on a program that suits your level, respect fatigue with deloads and sleep, modify rather than stop when something niggles, ramp up with warm-up sets, and train the supporting muscles of the upper back, hips and trunk.\n\nA pop or sudden severe pain, radiating pain or numbness, pain lasting more than a couple of weeks, or pain that recurs with the same lift is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
